{"full":"hf:build-small-hackathon/android-skill-router","spaceId":"build-small-hackathon/android-skill-router","name":"Android Skill Router","source":"huggingface","description":"Natural language → Android automation skill → UI trajectory","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","build-small-hackathon","track:backyard","track:wood","sponsor:modal","achievement:offbrand","achievement:fieldnotes","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-06-15T17:00:43.000Z","updated":"2026-06-15T22:20:33.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://build-small-hackathon-android-skill-router.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/android-skill-router","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T19:14:29.320Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T19:14:29.320Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T19:14:29.320Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"📱","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Build Small Hackathon — Backyard AI track · Modal sponsor","You say \"text mom on whatsapp i'm on my way\" — a voice assistant might web-search or shrug. Android Skill Router closes that gap with a 3B-parameter intent classifier that maps messy phone language to structured {skill, parameters} JSON, then loads a pre-recorded UI trajectory captured on a real Android device. It is the classifier layer of the Pocket Automator stack: record a flow once on your phone, route to it forever with a tiny model.","Tech: fine-tuned Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct via 4-bit QLoRA + SFT (Unsloth on Modal) → skill router → parameterized trajectory → Pocket Automator replay on device. Fifteen real Android flows expand to 15k synthetic intent examples for training; inference runs on Modal, demo UI on Gradio."],"features":["Blog post: Hugging Face Blog — Android Skill Router","Demo video: YouTube Short","Social post: Twitter/X","Live Space: android-skill-router","Android recorder: Pocket Automator"],"so